1
00:00:25,266 --> 00:00:27,852
You better be careful if you
don't want your heart broken.

2
00:00:29,222 --> 00:00:30,187
Why?

3
00:00:30,622 --> 00:00:31,831
Is he really a red flag?

4
00:00:32,078 --> 00:00:34,789
All I know is he’s
a walking heartbreak.

5
00:00:34,789 --> 00:00:37,000
There’s no chance
of commitment with him.

6
00:00:37,876 --> 00:00:39,044
I should go.

7
00:00:39,377 --> 00:00:40,587
How will you get home?

8
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,714
Come on, I'll take you home.

9
00:00:43,094 --> 00:00:44,096
It’s so early.

10
00:00:44,121 --> 00:00:46,290
Is this how you invite your FWBs?

11
00:00:46,843 --> 00:00:48,595
For the record, this is the first time.

12
00:00:48,595 --> 00:00:52,974
And you're the first girl
I've ever invited to my condo in BGC.

13
00:00:53,224 --> 00:00:53,975
But okay,

14
00:00:53,975 --> 00:00:56,227
if you wanna come home to my place,
I mean, I'm still down for that.

15
00:00:57,645 --> 00:00:58,772
It looks good on you.

16
00:00:59,647 --> 00:01:00,642
Do you have a crush on me?

17
00:01:12,261 --> 00:01:14,638
Meet me in Yesterday. 8PM, Wednesday.

18
00:01:14,996 --> 00:01:16,247
See you in Yesterday.

19
00:02:48,379 --> 00:02:49,421
Shan!

20
00:02:57,974 --> 00:02:58,933
Yes?

21
00:03:01,477 --> 00:03:02,896
How are your grades?

22
00:03:03,875 --> 00:03:06,628
I hope you get good grades, at least.

23
00:03:07,775 --> 00:03:09,611
Your tuition fee is so expensive.

24
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:12,864
Did you really just ask me
to come here for that?

25
00:03:14,157 --> 00:03:15,379
Why not?

26
00:03:15,992 --> 00:03:18,161
I’m the one paying for your tuition.

27
00:03:21,206 --> 00:03:22,540
Are you serious?

28
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:24,457
Fine. If you want
to see my grades, here.

29
00:03:28,129 --> 00:03:32,759
If you fail even once,

30
00:03:33,461 --> 00:03:35,922
you’ll be paying for your own tuition.

31
00:03:37,263 --> 00:03:39,098
I don’t want my money wasted.

32
00:03:40,308 --> 00:03:41,309
Are you broke?

33
00:03:43,228 --> 00:03:45,355
Is your business not doing well?

34
00:03:50,693 --> 00:03:52,904
It’s none of your fucking business.

35
00:03:59,369 --> 00:04:00,286
Why?

36
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:02,830
Are you still expecting your shares?

37
00:04:03,915 --> 00:04:05,124
You won’t get anything anymore.

38
00:04:05,458 --> 00:04:07,919
Everything your mom gave you back then,

39
00:04:07,919 --> 00:04:08,419
that’s all you get.

40
00:04:08,753 --> 00:04:09,587
That’s it.

41
00:04:10,713 --> 00:04:12,298
Do you really want to talk about shares?

42
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,259
Because if we’re talking about shares,

43
00:04:14,259 --> 00:04:16,511
I also have a right to the Ledezma group.

44
00:04:17,095 --> 00:04:18,054
And we both know,

45
00:04:18,054 --> 00:04:19,639
if it wasn’t because of mom,

46
00:04:20,175 --> 00:04:22,636
you wouldn’t be
who you are now, right?

47
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:26,980
Fuck you!

48
00:04:29,065 --> 00:04:30,817
I built this company myself.

49
00:04:31,276 --> 00:04:35,029
Your mom didn’t contribute
anything except being a bitch.

50
00:04:36,656 --> 00:04:37,532
Get out!

51
00:04:41,786 --> 00:04:42,954
Fucking rude.

52
00:05:20,992 --> 00:05:22,118
Shan!

53
00:05:35,313 --> 00:05:36,397
What are you doing here?

54
00:05:36,507 --> 00:05:38,760
Hiro told us to check on you.
Come here. What happened?

55
00:05:39,504 --> 00:05:40,922
It’s okay. I just had a fight.

56
00:05:41,126 --> 00:05:42,419
With your dad again?

57
00:05:44,474 --> 00:05:46,184
But don’t worry, I’m okay.

58
00:05:46,517 --> 00:05:47,643
Really, I’m okay.

59
00:05:47,727 --> 00:05:49,395
You know you can call us, right?

60
00:05:49,562 --> 00:05:50,313
Anytime.

61
00:05:50,742 --> 00:05:52,452
Yeah, I know. Thank you.

62
00:05:52,690 --> 00:05:54,859
But sorry, okay?
I really need to leave.

63
00:05:57,612 --> 00:05:58,863
I’m just really late.

64
00:05:58,863 --> 00:05:59,739
Okay, I’ll—

65
00:05:59,947 --> 00:06:01,032
Wait. For what?

66
00:06:01,032 --> 00:06:03,034
I’ll message you.
I’ll message you, guys. Okay?

67
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,454
Please.

68
00:06:44,826 --> 00:06:45,618
Alex.

69
00:06:45,618 --> 00:06:46,035
Sir.

70
00:06:46,035 --> 00:06:48,204
Oh no, sir…
What happened?

71
00:06:48,204 --> 00:06:49,497
Are you okay?

72
00:06:49,789 --> 00:06:50,915
Yeah, I’m okay.

73
00:06:51,666 --> 00:06:53,209
Did you see Kierra?

74
00:06:53,317 --> 00:06:55,819
Ms. Kierra? She already left.

75
00:06:56,358 --> 00:06:58,818
She was waiting
over there for quite a while.

76
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,501
Hold on, sir, I’ll get you an ice pack.

77
00:07:17,817 --> 00:07:19,318
<i>Sorry, I was late. </i>

78
00:07:19,928 --> 00:07:21,712
<i>Should I just go near your place?</i>

79
00:07:42,766 --> 00:07:44,454
<i>I’m really sorry about earlier.</i>

80
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:49,861
<i>Let me know, maybe we can</i>
<i>try a cafe near your condo?</i>

81
00:07:50,516 --> 00:07:51,851
<i>Good morning, Kierra.</i>

82
00:07:52,268 --> 00:07:53,644
<i>Are you free later?</i>

83
00:08:08,534 --> 00:08:09,775
Well, I guess that’s it.

84
00:09:18,312 --> 00:09:20,231
Can I try drawing, too?

85
00:09:22,483 --> 00:09:24,859
I dare you.

86
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,941
Wow, you’re really good.

87
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:29,907
Architecture really is your thing, huh?

88
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:34,036
Come on, I’ve wanted
it since I was little.

89
00:09:34,161 --> 00:09:35,079
Just like you.

90
00:09:36,027 --> 00:09:36,983
Yeah…

91
00:09:37,623 --> 00:09:39,333
But I’d rather be a painter.

92
00:09:41,794 --> 00:09:43,421
Why didn’t you take up painting then?

93
00:09:43,713 --> 00:09:46,841
I mean, you definitely
got your dad’s talent.

94
00:09:48,801 --> 00:09:52,430
Architecture is the practical choice.

95
00:09:58,436 --> 00:09:59,617
- You know…
- Hmm?

96
00:10:01,355 --> 00:10:03,024
You can still paint, you know.

97
00:10:03,357 --> 00:10:04,942
When you’re able to balance both.

98
00:10:05,074 --> 00:10:07,702
I mean, you don’t have to rush it.

99
00:10:07,727 --> 00:10:10,398
Besides, I think everything
will fall into place.

100
00:10:12,533 --> 00:10:15,286
Wow. Where did you read that?

101
00:10:15,286 --> 00:10:16,287
Right?

102
00:10:16,287 --> 00:10:17,330
But yeah,

103
00:10:18,039 --> 00:10:20,593
when I have free time,
I can still paint.

104
00:10:20,833 --> 00:10:21,667
Mhmm.

105
00:10:21,667 --> 00:10:24,837
And me, I’ll be your first fan, Ke.

106
00:10:24,837 --> 00:10:27,298
I can even pay the down payment
for your painting now.

107
00:10:27,298 --> 00:10:28,257
Whatever!

108
00:10:28,752 --> 00:10:29,545
But fine.

109
00:10:30,509 --> 00:10:32,678
You’re treating me if we
go out to drink this weekend.

110
00:10:33,054 --> 00:10:35,222
You’re such an idiot.
We’re really drinking this weekend.

111
00:10:35,389 --> 00:10:36,682
It’s Sam’s birthday.

112
00:10:37,266 --> 00:10:40,269
I think she’s also
introducing her boyfriend.

113
00:10:41,145 --> 00:10:43,689
She probably invited
all her friends, didn’t she?

114
00:10:44,398 --> 00:10:47,026
Of course, everyone.
You know Sam.

115
00:10:47,943 --> 00:10:50,446
Sam, do you know
someone named Ciandrei?

116
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:52,323
Well, he’s my friend but—

117
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,409
You better be careful if you
don't want your heart broken.

118
00:10:56,118 --> 00:10:58,746
I don’t think I’m
available this weekend.

119
00:10:58,746 --> 00:10:59,747
Huh?

120
00:11:00,081 --> 00:11:01,248
That’s not allowed.

121
00:11:01,415 --> 00:11:04,251
We’re not allowed to
not be there. We need to go.

122
00:11:04,752 --> 00:11:05,920
We all have to be there.

123
00:11:19,308 --> 00:11:21,727
Happy Birthday!

124
00:11:21,727 --> 00:11:22,186
Luna!

125
00:11:23,479 --> 00:11:26,649
Sevirous can’t make it,
so it's just going to be Ke and Via.

126
00:11:26,649 --> 00:11:27,191
It’s okay.

127
00:11:27,191 --> 00:11:28,859
Happy birthday!

128
00:11:28,859 --> 00:11:29,819
Thank you.

129
00:11:29,819 --> 00:11:32,697
- Happy birthday!
- Thank you, girls.

130
00:11:32,697 --> 00:11:33,948
Thank you for coming.

131
00:11:36,117 --> 00:11:37,785
Kalix is not here. Don’t worry.

132
00:11:39,745 --> 00:11:41,539
It’s not like I’m looking for him.

133
00:11:42,456 --> 00:11:46,210
Not looking ‘cause you don’t want to
see him, or because you do want to?

134
00:11:46,210 --> 00:11:48,379
I said I’m not looking for him!

135
00:11:49,463 --> 00:11:51,132
So? Are you introducing
someone to us?

136
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:52,967
I wouldn’t want to waste my outfit.

137
00:11:52,967 --> 00:11:55,302
I love this song! Girls, let's dance!

138
00:11:55,302 --> 00:11:57,179
Come on! Hurry, let’s dance!

139
00:11:57,179 --> 00:11:57,722
Okay, fine!

140
00:11:57,722 --> 00:12:00,099
Come on, come on. We’ll get to that later.

141
00:12:03,310 --> 00:12:04,311
Happy Birthday!

142
00:12:04,311 --> 00:12:05,312
Thank you.

143
00:12:22,204 --> 00:12:23,122
Oh, yeah!

144
00:12:24,039 --> 00:12:24,832
Thank you.

145
00:12:29,253 --> 00:12:29,920
- [LUNA] Don’t leave me!
- [SHAN] Wait!

146
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,255
- [SAM] Hey.
- [KIERRA] Sorry, Sam. I’m leaving.

147
00:12:31,505 --> 00:12:32,506
- [SAM] Huh? Why?
- [SHAN] Wait!

148
00:12:32,506 --> 00:12:33,549
- [LUNA] Hey—
- [SHAN] Sorry.

149
00:12:33,549 --> 00:12:35,342
[LUNA] Ke! Don’t leave me! Ke!

150
00:12:35,342 --> 00:12:36,927
What? What’s happening?

151
00:12:39,889 --> 00:12:40,556
Via?

152
00:12:40,556 --> 00:12:41,682
Larkin, what are you doing?

153
00:12:42,683 --> 00:12:43,368
What the—

154
00:12:44,268 --> 00:12:45,095
Hey!

155
00:12:45,853 --> 00:12:46,645
Wow.

156
00:12:47,354 --> 00:12:48,856
I’m so confused right now.

157
00:12:52,735 --> 00:12:53,555
Ke.

158
00:12:53,819 --> 00:12:54,445
Ke.

159
00:12:56,906 --> 00:12:58,032
Can we talk?

160
00:12:58,616 --> 00:13:01,786
I only came here
hoping I could catch you.

161
00:13:02,828 --> 00:13:03,746
Wait, wait.

162
00:13:03,906 --> 00:13:04,991
- Hey!
- Ke.

163
00:13:05,594 --> 00:13:07,513
Wait. Ke, do you know this guy?

164
00:13:07,958 --> 00:13:08,768
What’s wrong with you?

165
00:13:08,793 --> 00:13:10,836
Ke, go over there. I’ll handle this.

166
00:13:11,378 --> 00:13:13,172
Luna, you go first.

167
00:13:13,601 --> 00:13:14,853
We just need to talk.

168
00:13:14,924 --> 00:13:16,050
Do you know him?

169
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:20,721
If you do anything to
my cousin, I’ll find you, okay?

170
00:13:20,846 --> 00:13:22,848
So you better be careful,
do you understand?

171
00:13:26,352 --> 00:13:27,228
Call me, okay?

172
00:13:27,228 --> 00:13:28,229
Mhmm.

173
00:13:36,612 --> 00:13:37,822
Are you mad at me?

174
00:13:38,447 --> 00:13:40,533
Why would I be mad at you?
Did you do something?

175
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:45,579
I’m sorry I was late the other day.

176
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,916
I did go, but I missed you there.

177
00:13:49,959 --> 00:13:52,878
You’re not answering
my calls and texts either.

178
00:13:53,921 --> 00:13:55,256
So why were you late?

179
00:14:00,511 --> 00:14:03,556
There was an emergency.

180
00:14:04,974 --> 00:14:06,225
Emergency.

181
00:14:06,684 --> 00:14:08,060
What kind of emergency?

182
00:14:11,313 --> 00:14:13,023
You know what,
don’t even answer that.

183
00:14:13,065 --> 00:14:13,774
But Ke…

184
00:14:13,774 --> 00:14:14,441
No.

185
00:14:14,525 --> 00:14:15,818
It was my fault.

186
00:14:16,402 --> 00:14:18,654
Because I believed
all those things you said.

187
00:14:19,697 --> 00:14:22,116
I almost forgot
what kind of guy you are.

188
00:14:24,034 --> 00:14:25,411
What kind of guy am I?

189
00:14:26,537 --> 00:14:27,631
A lying jerk.

190
00:14:31,130 --> 00:14:33,132
You’re just playing with people.

191
00:14:33,919 --> 00:14:35,754
You have no respect.

192
00:14:37,464 --> 00:14:40,134
As long as it’s not your
time being wasted, you’re fine with it.

193
00:14:42,094 --> 00:14:45,472
You like fucking around and
disguising your acts as jokes.

194
00:14:48,267 --> 00:14:50,185
Right? That’s the kind of guy you are.

195
00:14:55,065 --> 00:14:56,275
That day.

196
00:14:57,693 --> 00:14:58,611
My Dad...

197
00:15:05,826 --> 00:15:06,702
Nevermind.

198
00:15:08,621 --> 00:15:09,914
Be careful going home.

199
00:15:11,624 --> 00:15:12,811
I’m sorry.

200
00:15:29,224 --> 00:15:32,139
When I was young, my dad said
I should grow up like him

201
00:15:34,855 --> 00:15:37,460
so I could understand everything he does.

202
00:15:39,497 --> 00:15:41,772
Because if I grow up like my mom,

203
00:15:42,652 --> 00:15:44,936
he said I’d just be a lying,
pathetic bitch like her.

204
00:15:48,077 --> 00:15:49,624
I don’t know who I take after.

205
00:15:51,830 --> 00:15:54,421
You are neither your dad nor your mom.

206
00:15:56,919 --> 00:15:58,929
You are you, Shan.

207
00:16:02,341 --> 00:16:05,260
What if I inherited
all of their bad traits?

208
00:16:07,262 --> 00:16:12,977
Because now, I’m starting to hurt other
people because of my problems.

209
00:16:13,417 --> 00:16:16,873
The same way they hurt me
because of their own problems.

210
00:16:19,692 --> 00:16:21,835
Did something happen recently?

211
00:16:31,659 --> 00:16:33,061
I don’t like lying.

212
00:16:35,207 --> 00:16:38,061
But I guess it’s much easier
that way than opening up.

213
00:16:39,461 --> 00:16:40,749
I understand.

214
00:16:42,328 --> 00:16:45,046
Being vulnerable sometimes is scary.

215
00:16:46,593 --> 00:16:50,180
But not being able to open up
doesn’t make you a bad person.

216
00:16:50,973 --> 00:16:52,936
Why are you scared to open up?

217
00:16:56,603 --> 00:16:58,230
I don’t know, Doc.

218
00:17:00,232 --> 00:17:02,026
Maybe I’m scared.

219
00:17:03,902 --> 00:17:06,413
I’m scared that they’ll know the real me.

220
00:17:08,615 --> 00:17:10,874
What if they can’t accept who I am?

221
00:17:16,498 --> 00:17:18,679
I see a recurring pattern here.

222
00:17:20,836 --> 00:17:22,921
Your fear of being fully known.

223
00:17:23,505 --> 00:17:27,968
And because of this, you struggle
to form close relationships.

224
00:17:30,095 --> 00:17:32,556
But this is something you can work on.

225
00:17:33,515 --> 00:17:35,893
The first step is to let those people in,

226
00:17:36,935 --> 00:17:38,701
even if it takes a while.

227
00:17:40,103 --> 00:17:42,614
This is the best way to build trust.

228
00:18:33,546 --> 00:18:34,464
So…

229
00:18:37,329 --> 00:18:39,706
Who was that guy the other night?

230
00:18:40,958 --> 00:18:43,043
You know that guy from Taft?

231
00:18:45,045 --> 00:18:45,796
No—

232
00:18:46,755 --> 00:18:48,007
Yeah, I just know him.

233
00:18:48,298 --> 00:18:50,384
Oh, you just know him, huh…

234
00:18:50,891 --> 00:18:53,269
Yeah. I’m just going to jog, okay?

235
00:18:53,294 --> 00:18:54,211
Okay.

236
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:56,839
Wait!

237
00:18:58,649 --> 00:19:01,110
How did you know
that he’s from Taft?

238
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:10,831
Can I kiss you?

239
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,252
Let’s kiss.

240
00:19:27,838 --> 00:19:31,563
Okay, I’ll tell you since it’s better
you hear it from me than from him.

241
00:19:31,592 --> 00:19:32,426
What?

242
00:19:33,844 --> 00:19:36,805
This happened before…
before Kalix, okay?

243
00:19:36,805 --> 00:19:38,932
- What I’m trying to say is...
- What is it?

244
00:19:39,141 --> 00:19:41,226
I was drunk back then, and then...

245
00:19:41,226 --> 00:19:45,606
I kissed him because I was kind
of trying to make Kalix jealous, and—

246
00:19:45,606 --> 00:19:47,316
I also didn’t know you’d meet each other—

247
00:19:47,316 --> 00:19:49,401
Ke, I’m so sorry, Ke.

248
00:19:49,401 --> 00:19:50,986
I’m really sorry! I didn’t really—

249
00:19:50,986 --> 00:19:54,448
Ke, I’m sorry, Ke. Don’t be mad.

250
00:19:54,823 --> 00:19:57,159
- Ke.
- So, he kissed you?

251
00:19:58,035 --> 00:20:01,997
Wow, it seems like he’s really
preyed on almost everyone, huh.

252
00:20:01,997 --> 00:20:03,540
I didn’t even know his name back then.

253
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,792
And Ke, don’t fight over this, okay?

254
00:20:05,792 --> 00:20:06,919
Even though I know you
two are already fighting.

255
00:20:06,919 --> 00:20:08,212
Are you mad?

256
00:20:08,962 --> 00:20:10,672
- Ke.
- It doesn’t bother me, Luna.

257
00:20:10,672 --> 00:20:11,715
Really?

258
00:20:11,715 --> 00:20:13,217
Yeah, I’m just going to jog, okay.

259
00:20:13,634 --> 00:20:15,260
Ke, you’re mad, though.

260
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:16,595
I’m just going to jog.

261
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:17,429
Ke.

262
00:20:17,429 --> 00:20:19,640
It doesn’t bother me. It’s okay.

263
00:20:27,986 --> 00:20:29,654
No. I’m not going in.

264
00:20:29,733 --> 00:20:30,901
You’re not going in.

265
00:20:31,944 --> 00:20:32,743
Kierra.

266
00:20:32,942 --> 00:20:34,235
Roel, I’ll be quick.

267
00:20:35,489 --> 00:20:36,114
Hey.

268
00:20:37,047 --> 00:20:37,715
Elyse?

269
00:20:37,832 --> 00:20:39,041
Do you live around here?

270
00:20:39,451 --> 00:20:41,370
Yeah, I live nearby.
What are you doing here?

271
00:20:41,578 --> 00:20:42,788
I’m just meeting someone.

272
00:20:44,206 --> 00:20:45,249
Okay, I’ll go ahead.

273
00:20:45,249 --> 00:20:46,416
Okay. Nice to see you.

274
00:20:46,625 --> 00:20:47,292
Alright.

275
00:20:58,679 --> 00:21:00,055
- Shan.
- Ely.

276
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,897
Why are you here?
It’s still too early.

277
00:21:09,064 --> 00:21:12,734
Shan, you haven’t been answering
your texts since you fought with Dad.

278
00:21:13,402 --> 00:21:14,111
Dad?

279
00:21:14,444 --> 00:21:15,279
Brother?

280
00:21:15,654 --> 00:21:16,738
Are they siblings?

281
00:21:20,284 --> 00:21:21,368
Can I look at it?

282
00:21:22,286 --> 00:21:23,787
Okay, it’s good.

283
00:21:23,812 --> 00:21:25,355
I can’t see the bruise anymore.

284
00:21:26,310 --> 00:21:27,478
Thank you, Ely.

285
00:21:27,624 --> 00:21:30,043
Thank you for checking up on me.
I appreciate you.

286
00:21:30,711 --> 00:21:31,837
Of course.

287
00:21:32,129 --> 00:21:33,005
Bruise?

288
00:21:34,464 --> 00:21:35,382
What’s that?

289
00:21:36,729 --> 00:21:37,938
I just had a fight.

290
00:21:38,927 --> 00:21:40,345
Do you want another escape?

291
00:21:41,346 --> 00:21:42,514
Where are we going?

292
00:21:42,723 --> 00:21:45,892
Where I go when I want to be alone.

293
00:21:47,644 --> 00:21:48,645
So why were you late?

294
00:21:49,730 --> 00:21:52,816
There was an emergency.

295
00:21:57,571 --> 00:21:59,364
There really was an emergency.

296
00:22:08,665 --> 00:22:09,618
Take care, okay?

297
00:22:18,091 --> 00:22:22,929
<i>Girl, can you order me an</i>
<i>iced matcha latte? I’ll treat you!</i>

298
00:22:37,569 --> 00:22:39,654
Good morning. What’s your order?

299
00:22:40,322 --> 00:22:42,991
We actually have a “buy one, take one”
promo until this weekend.

300
00:22:43,450 --> 00:22:44,910
Oh, okay.

301
00:22:45,619 --> 00:22:49,498
One iced latte and one iced matcha latte.

302
00:22:49,998 --> 00:22:51,958
Iced latte and matcha latte—

303
00:22:54,252 --> 00:22:55,962
Do you want anything else?

304
00:23:02,427 --> 00:23:03,387
That’s all.

305
00:23:04,638 --> 00:23:05,514
Thanks.

306
00:23:08,767 --> 00:23:09,684
Two hundred fifty.

307
00:23:17,150 --> 00:23:18,485
Thank you.

308
00:23:20,237 --> 00:23:21,071
Here.

309
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,366
I’ll just call your name
when your order’s ready.

310
00:23:36,128 --> 00:23:37,254
Order for Kierra.

311
00:23:43,468 --> 00:23:44,594
Enjoy your day.

312
00:23:45,199 --> 00:23:46,200
You too.

313
00:24:04,197 --> 00:24:06,616
<i>I’m sorry, come back.</i>

314
00:24:14,791 --> 00:24:15,552
Ke!

315
00:24:17,002 --> 00:24:17,646
Yeah?

316
00:24:17,961 --> 00:24:19,629
You look like you just saw a ghost.

317
00:24:19,754 --> 00:24:20,357
Huh?

318
00:24:20,714 --> 00:24:21,465
Huh?

319
00:24:23,389 --> 00:24:24,098
Where are you going?

320
00:24:24,123 --> 00:24:25,332
I’m heading out for a bit.

321
00:24:25,357 --> 00:24:26,733
I’m sleeping at Mama’s place tonight.

322
00:24:28,305 --> 00:24:30,015
Don’t forget about our dinner, okay?

323
00:24:30,015 --> 00:24:31,141
Yeah.

324
00:24:31,141 --> 00:24:32,309
Okay, sure. Love you. Bye.

325
00:24:32,934 --> 00:24:33,661
Bye.

326
00:25:03,048 --> 00:25:03,896
Alex.

327
00:25:04,216 --> 00:25:05,383
Did she already come by—

328
00:25:05,383 --> 00:25:06,510
Ma’am Kierra?

329
00:25:07,138 --> 00:25:08,053
- Yeah.
- She hasn’t yet.

330
00:25:08,053 --> 00:25:09,387
I haven’t seen her yet.

331
00:25:09,387 --> 00:25:11,306
But I’ll let you know if she stops by.

332
00:25:14,351 --> 00:25:15,352
Excuse me.

333
00:25:15,352 --> 00:25:16,353
What’s this?

334
00:25:16,353 --> 00:25:18,230
Can I also order one of those?

335
00:25:18,563 --> 00:25:20,690
Maybe we can order the barista, too.

336
00:25:23,318 --> 00:25:25,904
Sorry, but it’s not available.

337
00:25:26,196 --> 00:25:28,031
The drink or the one holding it?

338
00:25:30,992 --> 00:25:34,037
It’s the last day of our “buy one take
one” promo. Do you want to avail of it?

339
00:25:34,895 --> 00:25:36,814
Alex, you take care of them, okay?

340
00:25:37,499 --> 00:25:39,626
Hi ma’am, so this is our best seller.

341
00:25:49,135 --> 00:25:50,595
<i>Let’s have dinner tonight!</i>

342
00:26:02,732 --> 00:26:03,775
Let’s get a dessert?

343
00:26:03,822 --> 00:26:04,656
Dessert?

344
00:26:08,266 --> 00:26:09,846
Well?

345
00:26:11,366 --> 00:26:14,744
Wow, she’s really into what
she’s looking at. I know I’m pretty.

346
00:26:15,620 --> 00:26:16,329
It’s fine.

347
00:26:20,250 --> 00:26:21,835
His condo is close by.

348
00:26:22,385 --> 00:26:23,678
Huh? Who?

349
00:26:24,660 --> 00:26:25,995
Oh, Taft boy?

350
00:26:28,141 --> 00:26:31,227
Sorry, Ke. I didn’t know.
I’m just really craving the food here.

351
00:26:32,387 --> 00:26:33,324
Are you two good now?

352
00:26:36,789 --> 00:26:38,958
Oh, I know that look.

353
00:26:39,644 --> 00:26:41,605
Why don’t you just talk to each other?

354
00:26:41,605 --> 00:26:44,107
If you two just talked, you wouldn’t be
all up in your head right now.

355
00:26:44,292 --> 00:26:45,387
Common since.

356
00:26:45,657 --> 00:26:46,629
My god.

357
00:26:47,402 --> 00:26:48,737
Common sense.

358
00:26:49,070 --> 00:26:50,488
Common cents.

359
00:26:55,619 --> 00:26:57,120
What’s going on, bro?

360
00:26:58,580 --> 00:26:59,497
Nothing.

361
00:26:59,956 --> 00:27:00,749
Are you sure?

362
00:27:00,749 --> 00:27:01,652
Yeah.

363
00:27:03,126 --> 00:27:05,629
Wait, hold on. I’ll be right back.

364
00:27:05,629 --> 00:27:06,504
Where are you going?

365
00:27:07,672 --> 00:27:08,757
I just need to buy something.

366
00:27:09,174 --> 00:27:11,635
Cigarettes? You’re smoking again, man.

367
00:27:11,885 --> 00:27:12,719
I don’t smoke anymore.

368
00:27:12,719 --> 00:27:13,595
I’ll buy a froyo.

369
00:27:13,928 --> 00:27:14,721
Get me some, bro.

370
00:27:14,804 --> 00:27:15,764
I got you.

371
00:27:19,520 --> 00:27:20,354
<i>Funny.</i>

372
00:27:20,735 --> 00:27:22,362
<i>We’re so near each other right now.</i>

373
00:27:31,970 --> 00:27:33,388
<i>Look outside.</i>

374
00:27:41,755 --> 00:27:42,631
Luna.

375
00:27:43,333 --> 00:27:46,211
- I’m going to buy—
- You’re meeting with Taft boy?

376
00:27:48,338 --> 00:27:50,548
Ke, come on, we’re like sisters.

377
00:27:51,341 --> 00:27:53,718
You can tell me everything, seriously.

378
00:27:54,803 --> 00:27:55,762
Okay.

379
00:27:56,304 --> 00:27:57,555
We’ll just talk for a bit.

380
00:27:57,806 --> 00:27:58,556
- Okay.
- I’ll be right back.

381
00:27:58,556 --> 00:28:00,266
If you need backup, call me.

382
00:28:01,576 --> 00:28:02,369
Okay. I’ll be quick.

383
00:28:02,394 --> 00:28:03,269
Go.

384
00:28:15,073 --> 00:28:15,907
Hi.

385
00:28:18,993 --> 00:28:20,203
Let me make it up to you.

386
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:24,538
Can we get coffee or go out
or anything you want?

387
00:28:25,875 --> 00:28:28,044
Are you asking me out on a date again?

388
00:28:28,628 --> 00:28:30,380
Yes. A date.

389
00:28:30,405 --> 00:28:32,157
Then you’ll just ditch me again.

390
00:28:34,884 --> 00:28:36,845
I’m really sorry for
what happened last time.

391
00:28:37,637 --> 00:28:39,013
I couldn’t show myself to you.

392
00:28:41,182 --> 00:28:43,810
After what happened,
how can I trust you again?

393
00:28:46,765 --> 00:28:48,517
I know it’s not something
that happens right away.

394
00:28:49,044 --> 00:28:53,590
I know, but can you give me a chance?

395
00:28:55,697 --> 00:28:58,684
Am I letting myself
get played with again?

396
00:28:59,823 --> 00:29:01,492
I’m not playing with you.

397
00:29:03,353 --> 00:29:05,229
And I’ll never play you.

398
00:29:23,975 --> 00:29:24,809
How was it?

399
00:29:24,809 --> 00:29:25,852
So, are you two okay now?

400
00:29:27,266 --> 00:29:28,935
I said I’d think about it first.

401
00:29:30,899 --> 00:29:31,697
Right.

402
00:29:31,771 --> 00:29:34,273
You know, if he’s serious
about you, he’ll wait for you.

403
00:29:34,861 --> 00:29:37,405
Right? Okay, come on. Let’s go.

404
00:29:46,289 --> 00:29:47,373
Thank you.

405
00:30:14,234 --> 00:30:16,277
<i>Let’s have lunch here at home!</i>

406
00:30:17,017 --> 00:30:18,436
<i>Sorry, I can’t.</i>

407
00:30:18,837 --> 00:30:19,796
<i>Next time!</i>

408
00:30:37,966 --> 00:30:38,967
Yo, what’s up?

409
00:30:38,992 --> 00:30:39,721
Bro,

410
00:30:40,343 --> 00:30:43,721
where the fuck are you?
I’m only in Manila once in a while.

411
00:30:43,721 --> 00:30:46,808
Okay, okay. How about tomorrow?
Let’s go out tomorrow.

412
00:30:46,894 --> 00:30:50,252
You’re still in the waiting room, huh?

413
00:30:52,719 --> 00:30:54,846
All right, guys, just
enjoy yourselves, okay?

414
00:30:54,941 --> 00:30:56,317
Have fun. Take care.

415
00:30:56,985 --> 00:30:58,111
Bye.

416
00:31:18,949 --> 00:31:20,033
<i>Hi, Kierra!</i>

417
00:31:20,374 --> 00:31:22,710
<i>Just wanted to ask if you’re free today?</i>

418
00:31:23,036 --> 00:31:25,010
<i>Or let me know when you’re available.</i>

419
00:31:38,354 --> 00:31:39,522
What are you doing?

420
00:31:40,522 --> 00:31:41,635
Don’t rush her.

421
00:31:44,268 --> 00:31:46,019
She might not reply anyway.

422
00:32:08,045 --> 00:32:10,580
<i>Hi, I’m free at 6 today.</i>

423
00:32:12,414 --> 00:32:13,206
<i>Okay.</i>

424
00:32:13,389 --> 00:32:15,850
<i>I’ll pick you up at 6! See you!</i>

425
00:32:29,345 --> 00:32:31,263
You’re gonna trust him again?

426
00:32:33,361 --> 00:32:34,988
Don’t be such an idiot.

427
00:32:36,668 --> 00:32:37,455
Okay?

428
00:32:38,145 --> 00:32:39,605
One last chance.

429
00:32:43,257 --> 00:32:44,092
Ke.

430
00:32:44,404 --> 00:32:46,698
Oh. Where are you going?

431
00:32:47,637 --> 00:32:48,721
To BGC.

432
00:32:50,682 --> 00:32:51,705
You’re going to meet him?

433
00:32:54,185 --> 00:32:54,978
Okay.

434
00:32:55,668 --> 00:32:57,211
Are you sure you’re ready?

435
00:32:58,439 --> 00:32:59,408
Can you handle it?

436
00:32:59,983 --> 00:33:01,192
It’s just a distraction.

437
00:33:02,860 --> 00:33:03,611
Okay.

438
00:33:03,793 --> 00:33:05,545
Okay, then. Here you go.

439
00:33:07,490 --> 00:33:09,492
Just call me if you need anything.

440
00:33:10,243 --> 00:33:13,287
Just turn on your
location on your phone, okay?

441
00:33:13,866 --> 00:33:15,284
I’ll let Sam know, too.

442
00:33:15,873 --> 00:33:16,557
Okay.

443
00:33:16,582 --> 00:33:17,317
Okay?

444
00:33:18,543 --> 00:33:19,335
Take care.

445
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:21,796
Let’s just fix—

446
00:33:22,630 --> 00:33:23,881
Let’s fix this.

447
00:33:41,024 --> 00:33:41,816
Hi, Kierra.

448
00:33:42,650 --> 00:33:43,818
Hi. Have you been waiting long?

449
00:33:44,551 --> 00:33:45,969
No, I just got here.

450
00:33:46,484 --> 00:33:47,496
Where should we go?

451
00:33:47,572 --> 00:33:49,532
I prepared a few things to do tonight,

452
00:33:49,532 --> 00:33:51,826
but if you have something in mind,
we can do that instead.

453
00:33:51,826 --> 00:33:53,119
No, let’s do your plan.

454
00:33:56,142 --> 00:33:57,145
You look nice.

455
00:33:58,825 --> 00:33:59,668
Is it okay?

456
00:34:00,313 --> 00:34:01,356
It suits you.

457
00:34:04,130 --> 00:34:05,590
You look nice, too.

458
00:34:07,675 --> 00:34:08,843
Let’s go.

459
00:34:16,491 --> 00:34:19,994
Sam, keep track of Ke, okay?

460
00:34:21,064 --> 00:34:26,949
I’ll call Via too, and let anyone
who might be close know.

461
00:34:53,471 --> 00:34:54,430
Do you like your book?

462
00:34:55,014 --> 00:34:56,766
Yeah, I do. I got two.

463
00:34:57,642 --> 00:34:59,102
What are they about?

464
00:34:59,811 --> 00:35:04,357
One’s about architecture,
and the other’s a rom-com.

465
00:35:05,108 --> 00:35:05,900
Nice.

466
00:35:05,900 --> 00:35:06,692
Yeah.

467
00:35:07,130 --> 00:35:08,590
- Here—
- Sorry, Ke.

468
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:11,739
I’m just going to the bathroom.
I’ll be quick; I’ll be right back.

469
00:35:11,864 --> 00:35:12,490
Okay.

470
00:35:12,683 --> 00:35:13,350
Wait for me.

471
00:35:13,375 --> 00:35:13,959
Okay.

472
00:35:17,036 --> 00:35:17,745
Hey!

473
00:35:18,193 --> 00:35:19,069
Shan!

474
00:35:19,664 --> 00:35:20,331
Miguel.

475
00:35:21,833 --> 00:35:23,334
Nice seeing you here.

476
00:35:27,226 --> 00:35:29,407
Look at you. Dressed to impress, huh.

477
00:35:29,674 --> 00:35:30,967
Hot stuff!

478
00:35:32,301 --> 00:35:32,927
Who’s with you?

479
00:35:32,927 --> 00:35:33,678
Who are you with?

480
00:35:36,305 --> 00:35:37,172
Girlfriend?

481
00:35:37,974 --> 00:35:39,008
Is that your new girl?

482
00:35:39,892 --> 00:35:41,144
Introduce me, come on.

483
00:35:41,959 --> 00:35:45,838
I think you should introduce me
to your new partner, don’t you think?

484
00:35:46,065 --> 00:35:46,941
It’s a bit rude.

485
00:35:49,853 --> 00:35:52,105
And I think she just left you.

486
00:36:07,003 --> 00:36:07,461
Ke.

487
00:36:07,461 --> 00:36:08,045
Why?

488
00:36:10,548 --> 00:36:11,549
Ke, where are you?

489
00:36:12,967 --> 00:36:14,719
Luna, help—

490
00:36:15,928 --> 00:36:17,680
Help me, Luna. I—

491
00:36:18,823 --> 00:36:20,408
Wait there, okay?

492
00:36:20,433 --> 00:36:21,642
Let me check your location.

493
00:36:22,643 --> 00:36:23,376
I don’t—

494
00:36:24,145 --> 00:36:25,521
I don’t know about this.

495
00:36:25,938 --> 00:36:27,440
Okay. I have your location now.

496
00:36:27,857 --> 00:36:29,066
Don’t go anywhere, okay?

497
00:36:29,066 --> 00:36:30,276
Sam’s on her way.

498
00:36:30,735 --> 00:36:33,362
Okay. Everything’s gonna be okay, Ke.
Everything’s gonna be okay.

499
00:36:57,303 --> 00:36:57,887
Ke?

500
00:36:58,823 --> 00:37:00,575
Ke, it’s okay.

501
00:37:03,017 --> 00:37:03,851
It’s okay.

502
00:37:04,477 --> 00:37:06,479
It’s okay. I’m here, you're safe.

503
00:37:06,896 --> 00:37:08,522
Calm down. It's okay.

504
00:37:08,898 --> 00:37:09,732
Sam.

505
00:37:12,568 --> 00:37:13,444
You're safe.

506
00:37:14,805 --> 00:37:15,639
Sam.

507
00:37:49,021 --> 00:37:50,273
Did you find her?

508
00:37:51,464 --> 00:37:52,507
No, bro.

509
00:37:56,737 --> 00:37:58,364
She just vanished into thin air.

510
00:38:00,074 --> 00:38:02,159
Was I dating a ghost all along?

511
00:38:04,912 --> 00:38:08,874
If you weren’t dating, how could
you say you love her?

512
00:38:10,918 --> 00:38:13,212
You need to be in the
position to understand.

513
00:38:15,589 --> 00:38:17,675
I can’t put it into words.

514
00:38:21,375 --> 00:38:27,215
I didn’t even want to commit because
I knew I'd eventually move to the US.

515
00:38:28,573 --> 00:38:35,497
But with Yanna, I took the risk
even though I knew I’d get hurt.

516
00:38:46,716 --> 00:38:47,968
Why is it special?

517
00:38:49,679 --> 00:38:52,140
Because I only made it for you.

518
00:38:52,669 --> 00:38:54,319
You haven’t used
it in a while, but you

519
00:38:54,343 --> 00:38:56,343
always keep an extra
helmet ready for a girl?

520
00:38:56,841 --> 00:38:59,135
I haven't given any
girl a ride on this yet.

521
00:38:59,542 --> 00:39:02,420
You know what, it’s actually
my first time bringing someone here.

522
00:39:02,762 --> 00:39:04,305
You can't fool me.

523
00:39:04,972 --> 00:39:05,890
I’m telling the truth.

524
00:39:06,288 --> 00:39:08,290
Is this how you invite your FWBs?

525
00:39:08,734 --> 00:39:10,444
For the record, this is the first time.

526
00:39:10,469 --> 00:39:15,099
And you're the first girl I've ever
invited to my condo in BGC.

527
00:39:16,382 --> 00:39:19,373
You know, it’s my first
time sleeping over with

528
00:39:19,397 --> 00:39:22,388
a girl without ending up
in the same bed as her.

529
00:39:26,160 --> 00:39:27,953
You? How’s that girl—

530
00:39:27,953 --> 00:39:29,512
uh… Kierra.

531
00:39:33,222 --> 00:39:38,853
I asked her out this Sunday,
but I’m still waiting for her reply.

532
00:39:40,124 --> 00:39:42,293
Bro, it’s only Monday.

533
00:39:42,525 --> 00:39:44,443
Yeah, I know.

534
00:39:44,468 --> 00:39:47,346
But who knows, she might text.
I need to confirm right away.

535
00:39:48,974 --> 00:39:50,083
You’re one to talk, though.

536
00:39:50,218 --> 00:39:52,262
You’ve been waiting for Yanna for so long.

537
00:39:59,977 --> 00:40:02,004
I guess we’re both inside
the waiting room, huh?

538
00:40:08,911 --> 00:40:09,880
Willing to wait.

539
00:40:11,497 --> 00:40:13,207
I’m willing to wait for her, too.

540
00:40:28,722 --> 00:40:31,600
<i>Hi, I’m free at 6 today.</i>

541
00:40:32,601 --> 00:40:36,063
<i>Okay. I’ll pick you up at 6! See you!</i>

542
00:41:28,703 --> 00:41:29,833
You look nice.

543
00:41:31,965 --> 00:41:32,841
Is it okay?

544
00:41:33,489 --> 00:41:34,657
It suits you.

545
00:41:37,291 --> 00:41:38,848
Your outfit suits you, too.

546
00:41:48,158 --> 00:41:49,701
Sam, this is so hard.

547
00:41:50,471 --> 00:41:52,389
This is just so hard.

548
00:41:53,766 --> 00:41:56,060
Eat something first.
Do you still have a fever?

549
00:41:56,550 --> 00:41:57,926
Why don’t you guys go out for a bit?

550
00:41:58,020 --> 00:41:59,438
- She said you guys should go out.
- Just go out.

551
00:41:59,438 --> 00:42:00,262
Are you hungry?

552
00:42:00,593 --> 00:42:02,052
Let me stay here with you for now.

553
00:42:10,339 --> 00:42:14,135
So, you’re dreaming of the same scenario?

554
00:42:21,877 --> 00:42:23,337
Lopez.

555
00:42:24,880 --> 00:42:26,317
I’ve been nice to you, right?

556
00:42:27,007 --> 00:42:28,300
Be nice to me.

557
00:42:32,896 --> 00:42:34,398
Why are you alone?

558
00:42:36,128 --> 00:42:37,046
Don’t you have a date?

559
00:42:37,405 --> 00:42:38,323
A date?

560
00:42:39,353 --> 00:42:40,354
Poor you.

561
00:42:40,354 --> 00:42:43,065
Fine, I’ll be your date tonight.
